  "reasoning": "This is REC Limited (Rural Electrification Corporation), an NBFC/infrastructure finance company. As per the BANKS/NBFCs rule, 'Total Income' (Revenue from Operations + Other Income) is used as the top-line Revenue, reported as INR 39,230 Cr in FY2022 and INR 35,410 Cr in FY2021 (standalone figures from the five-year highlights table, consistent across all years). The 4-year CAGR from FY2018 (22,467 Cr) to FY2022 (39,230 Cr) is approximately 15%, while the latest YoY growth was ~10.8%, indicating no sharp anomaly \u2014 FY2020 showed a jump due to loan book expansion and FY2022 reflects normalizing post-COVID disbursements. A blended growth rate of ~14% was chosen for FY2023, stepping up to ~14-15% in FY2024-25, supported by: (1) REC's expanding loan book (from Rs 2.39 lakh Cr in FY2018 to Rs 3.85 lakh Cr in FY2022, ~13% CAGR), (2) government's strong push on power sector capex and renewables lending, (3) healthy capital adequacy of 23.61% providing headroom for growth, and (4) declining debt-equity ratio (7.40x to 6.41x) signaling improving leverage; net profit margins are assumed stable-to-improving as provisioning normalizes and operating leverage plays out."
